---
deadlock_detection: false
---

# hung_transcript: the open thread's first transcript read and its
# catch-ups when they are slow or never answer (go/tests/model/README.md).
# The twin of hung_requests (list poll, send, Stop), split from it because
# the two together were 7920 states and share no field.
# live_transcript_sync models these reads failing; this models them
# hanging. api.ts req() has no timeout, so a read the server accepts and
# never answers stays pending for as long as the tab lives.
#
# Page (app.tsx, the `selected` effect): opening a session GETs the whole
# transcript; while it is out the thread says "Loading transcript…", and
# only a failed read shows "Couldn't load this session" with Retry. A
# recorded event arms a 120 ms catch-up (GET ?since=), which does not
# wait for an earlier one still out; a failed catch-up sets `paused`
# ("Updates paused · last synced … · Retry") and re-arms on a 4 s..30 s
# backoff. `paused` is set only in the catch-up's .catch. Leaving the
# thread ends the effect: `live` goes false and answers to it are ignored.
#
# Fields (Thread role):
#   open      the session's thread is on screen
#   first     its first transcript read: none | out | hung | loaded | failed
#   catchup   the newest catch-up read: none | out | hung
#   timer     a catch-up timer is armed (an event's 120 ms, or the backoff)
#   behind    an event was recorded that no landed read has brought in
#   paused    "Updates paused · Retry" is on screen
#   recorded  an Event was recorded this walk: the ring replays a record
#             to every new subscriber, and the page arms its catch-up on it
#
# Abstractions: one event at a time (an event arrives only with no timer
# armed); the first read's answer does not clear `behind` (the event's own
# catch-up does, as in the product); a newer catch-up takes the slot of a
# hung one, which never answers anyway. Answer/Fail/Hang are the server's
# choice per request; a request that is out and not hung answers (fair)
# or fails.
#
# Fairness: the page's own steps (timers firing, answers to requests that
# are out) are strongly fair. The person (Open, Leave, Retry), the session
# (Event) and the network (Hang, Fail) are not.
#
# Corrections to the mapped model, from the code:
# - a hung catch-up is not the end: the next recorded event arms a new
#   catch-up that does not wait for the hung one. A hung LAST catch-up
#   (the turn's final event) is the one that stays silent.
# - a hung first read is left by leaving the thread; coming back (Open)
#   reads again. On the thread itself there is no Retry.
#
# Corrections from the server walk (mbt/hung_transcript_test.go):
# - opening the thread subscribes, and the ring replays the session's
#   last records to the new EventSource; each arms the 120 ms catch-up.
#   Open (and RetryFirst) arm the timer when the walk recorded an Event.
#   Records from before the walk are outside the model.
# - RetryFirst bumps loadTry, which re-runs the whole effect: the old
#   run's catch-up and timer are dropped, `paused` is cleared, the lines
#   start empty and the new first read is sent after every event so far,
#   so nothing is behind until the next one.
# - so "paused means behind" (PausedOnlyWhenBehind) does not hold: the
#   catch-up the replay arms can fail with nothing behind, and "Updates
#   paused" then shows over a transcript the first read will fill.
#   Open, Event, CatchUpFire, CatchUpAnswers, Leave, Open, CatchUpFire,
#   CatchUpFails. The claim is dropped; it is a false alarm, not a loss.
#
# The product does not meet the mapped claims; they are left out so the
# check stays green, each with the counterexample fizz gave when it was
# added (findings, not fixed here):
#
#   CatchUpStaleShown  not (catchup == "hung" and behind and not timer and not paused)
#     Open, Event, CatchUpFire, CatchUpHangs: the turn's last entry never
#     shows and the header does not say paused.
#   (liveness) LoadingEnds  always eventually not (open and first == "hung")
#     fizz's lasso ends with first == "hung" on the open thread (it
#     reached it through FirstFails, RetryFirst, FirstHangs):
#     "Loading transcript…" with no Retry for as long as the person stays.
#   (liveness) CaughtUp  always eventually not (open and behind and not paused)
#     fizz's lasso is events arriving forever (each catch-up answers
#     after the next event), which a live turn does; the silent one is
#     CatchUpStaleShown's path, behind forever and never paused.

role Thread:
    action Init:
        self.open = False
        self.first = "none"
        self.catchup = "none"
        self.timer = False
        self.behind = False
        self.paused = False
        self.recorded = False

    atomic action Open:
        require not self.open
        self.open = True
        self.first = "out"
        self.timer = self.recorded

    atomic action Leave:
        require self.open
        self.open = False
        self.first = "none"
        self.catchup = "none"
        self.timer = False
        self.behind = False
        self.paused = False

    atomic fair<strong> action FirstAnswers:
        require self.first == "out"
        self.first = "loaded"

    atomic action FirstFails:
        require self.first == "out"
        self.first = "failed"

    atomic action FirstHangs:
        require self.first == "out"
        self.first = "hung"

    # "Couldn't load this session · Retry" (setLoadTry): the effect again.
    atomic action RetryFirst:
        require self.first == "failed"
        self.first = "out"
        self.catchup = "none"
        self.timer = self.recorded
        self.behind = False
        self.paused = False

    # A recorded event on the open session's stream arms the catch-up.
    atomic action Event:
        require self.open and not self.timer
        self.timer = True
        self.behind = True
        self.recorded = True

    atomic fair<strong> action CatchUpFire:
        require self.timer
        self.timer = False
        self.catchup = "out"

    atomic fair<strong> action CatchUpAnswers:
        require self.catchup == "out"
        self.catchup = "none"
        self.paused = False
        # An event after this read was sent is still to come.
        self.behind = self.timer

    # .catch: paused, and a backoff re-arms the catch-up.
    atomic action CatchUpFails:
        require self.catchup == "out"
        self.catchup = "none"
        self.paused = True
        self.timer = True

    atomic action CatchUpHangs:
        require self.catchup == "out"
        self.catchup = "hung"

    # "Updates paused · Retry": clearTimeout, then a catch-up now.
    atomic action RetryCatchUp:
        require self.paused
        self.timer = False
        self.catchup = "out"

action Init:
    thread = Thread()

# "Updates paused" always has a way on: a catch-up armed or out, or the
# hung one its Retry replaces.
always assertion PausedHasAWayOn:
    return not thread.paused or thread.timer or thread.catchup != "none"

# A thread left behind holds nothing: its reads are ignored (`live`) and
# its timer cleared, so nothing of it can pause or load later.
always assertion ClosedThreadHoldsNothing:
    return thread.open or (thread.first == "none" and thread.catchup == "none" and not thread.timer and not thread.paused and not thread.behind)

# A read that is out and not hung is answered or reported.
always eventually assertion FirstReadSettles:
    return thread.first != "out"

always eventually assertion CatchUpSettles:
    return thread.catchup != "out"

# A failed catch-up (paused, timer armed) is retried without the person.
always eventually assertion BackoffFires:
    return not thread.timer
